+# IFRS S1/S2 Sustainability-Related Financial Disclosures
+
+# 1. General Requirements
+
+This section describes the basis on which the sustainability-related financial disclosures have been prepared, including the reporting period, currency, comparative information, connected information, and the key methodologies, estimates and judgements applied to climate-related disclosures.
+
+### Basis of preparation and scope of sustainability-related financial disclosures
+
+These sustainability-related financial disclosures are prepared to present fairly sustainability-related risks and opportunities that could reasonably be expected to affect the entityÔÇÖs prospects. Fair presentation is supported through disclosures that are complete, neutral and accurate, and through information that is comparable, verifiable, timely and understandable.
+
+The disclosures are structured to enable users to understand connections:
+
+- **Between sustainability-related risks and opportunities**ÔÇöfor example, how acute physical risks to mortgage collateral and chronic physical risks affecting agricultural counterparties can both influence credit risk through different transmission channels.
+- **Across the disclosure pillars**ÔÇögovernance, strategy, risk management, and metrics and targetsÔÇöby linking (i) how climate-related risks are monitored and reported, (ii) how scenario analysis is performed to assess resilience, and (iii) how performance is measured using emissions, financed emissions and selected portfolio indicators.
+
+### Reporting period and fiscal year
+
+The reporting year for these sustainability-related financial disclosures is **2024**. The fiscal year end is **31 December 2024**.
+
+### Reporting currency
+
+The reporting currency used in these sustainability-related financial disclosures is **euro (EUR)**.
+
+Where currency is used as a unit of measure (for example, climate-related capital expenditure and Tier 1 capital), amounts are presented in **EUR millions (EURm)**.
+
+### Comparative information
+
+Comparative information is provided for **2022** and **2023** where available and relevant to understanding performance and trends.
+
+The following table summarises selected climate-related financial and portfolio indicators presented on a comparable basis across the reporting year and comparative years.
+
