+Scope 1 emissions include fleet emissions.
+
+For Scope 2 market-based emissions, the market-based figure is sourced from utility invoice data that already reflects market-based accounting using grid emission factors adjusted for renewable energy certificates and power purchase agreements. Renewable energy certificate registry information is used for disclosure narrative and is not subtracted again during preparation, avoiding double-counting.
+
+### Financed emissions (Scope 3 Category 15)
+
+Financed emissions are a key metric used to monitor climate-related transition risk and the effectiveness of portfolio decarbonisation actions. We disclose financed emissions for corporate loans for 2022ÔÇô2024, and selected listed equity exposure metrics for 2024.
+
+#### Corporate loans ÔÇö financed emissions and portfolio size
+
+Financed emissions for corporate loans are calculated using a PCAF approach in which the bank attributes a share of a counterpartyÔÇÖs total greenhouse gas emissions based on the ratio of the bankÔÇÖs outstanding amount to the counterpartyÔÇÖs enterprise value including cash (EVIC). In plain language, this method allocates emissions in proportion to the bankÔÇÖs financing share of the counterparty.
+
+**Corporate loans ÔÇö financed emissions (tCOÔéée) and total loans (EURm)**
+
+| Reporting year | Financed emissions (tCOÔéée) | Total loans (EURm) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 2022 | 36,550,177.7 | 31,150.64 |
+| 2023 | 37,427,593.2 | 31,150.64 |
+| 2024 | 35,973,167.7 | 31,150.64 |
+
+For 2024, financed emissions from corporate loans were **35,973,167.7 tCOÔéée**.
+
+#### Listed equity ÔÇö exposure metrics and proxy input
+
+For listed equity positions, we apply a PCAF approach that attributes an investee share using the ratio of the investmentÔÇÖs market value to the issuerÔÇÖs EVIC. For the emissions-related input used in this calculation, **issuer revenue** is used as the proxy input in line with the referenced PCAF proxy approach.
