+### Financed emissions (Scope 3 Category 15)
+
+Financed emissions are a key metric used to monitor climate-related risk and performance associated with the entityÔÇÖs lending and investment activities.
+
+#### Financed emissions ÔÇö corporate loans
+
+Financed emissions from corporate loans are disclosed for 2022ÔÇô2024, together with the associated total loan exposure used in the calculation.
+
+**Financed emissions from corporate loans**
+
+| Reporting year | Total loans (EUR m) | Financed emissions (tCOÔéée) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 2022 | 31,150.64 | 36,550,177.7 |
+| 2023 | 31,150.64 | 37,427,593.2 |
+| 2024 | 31,150.64 | 35,973,167.7 |
+
+**Methodology (PCAF ÔÇö corporate loans).** Financed emissions for corporate loans are calculated in line with the Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF) Standard (section referenced as ┬ºB62). In plain terms, the entity attributes a share of a borrowerÔÇÖs total GHG emissions to the loan based on the proportion that the loanÔÇÖs outstanding amount represents relative to the borrowerÔÇÖs enterprise value including cash (EVIC). The attributed share is then aggregated across the loan portfolio.
+
+#### Financed emissions ÔÇö listed equity (proxy approach)
+
+For listed equity holdings reported for 2024, the entity applies a PCAF proxy approach that uses **issuer revenue** as the proxy input basis (referenced as PCAF Standard ┬ºB61 proxy). The proxy approach is applied by scaling the proxy input by the entityÔÇÖs share of the issuerÔÇÖs enterprise value including cash (EVIC), based on the market value of the holding.
