+The bankÔÇÖs climate-related strategy is shaped by the interaction of (i) transition risks affecting carbon-intensive sectors and technology pathways, (ii) physical risks affecting collateral and borrower performance, and (iii) opportunities in sustainable finance and advisory services. Scenario analysis indicates that resilience differs by pathway: orderly transition outcomes are assessed as manageable within existing buffers, while disorderly transition and hot house world pathways increase the importance of sector exposure limits, portfolio decarbonisation monitoring, and collateral-focused resilience mechanisms (including flood-zone overlays and EPC-based monitoring) across the medium term and long term.
