+### PCAF methodology for corporate loans (plain-language description)
+
+Financed emissions for corporate loans are calculated using an attribution approach aligned to the **Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF) Standard**. For each counterparty, the entity attributes a share of the counterpartyÔÇÖs total GHG emissions based on the proportion of the counterpartyÔÇÖs enterprise value represented by the entityÔÇÖs outstanding loan amount. In practical terms:
+
+- the entity determines the **outstanding loan amount**;
+- it compares this to the counterpartyÔÇÖs **enterprise value including cash (EVIC)** to derive an attribution factor; and
+- it applies that attribution factor to the counterpartyÔÇÖs **total GHG emissions** to estimate the emissions associated with the entityÔÇÖs financing.
+
