+#### Financed emissionsÔÇöcorporate loans
+
+For corporate loans, financed emissions are calculated in line with the **Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF) Standard (Section B62)**. In plain language, the approach attributes a share of a borrowerÔÇÖs total GHG emissions to the bank based on the bankÔÇÖs **outstanding loan amount** relative to the borrowerÔÇÖs **enterprise value including cash (EVIC)**.
+
+**Financed emissions from loans and advances**
+
+| Reporting year | Financed emissions (tCOÔéée) | Total loans (EUR m) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 2022 | 36,550,177.7 | 31,150.64 |
+| 2023 | 37,427,593.2 | 31,150.64 |
+| 2024 | 35,973,167.7 | 31,150.64 |
+
+The 2024 financed emissions from loans were **35,973,167.7 tCOÔéée** on total loans of **EUR 31,150.64 million**.
+
+#### Financed emissionsÔÇölisted equity (proxy input)
+
+For listed equity, the bank applies a PCAF-aligned approach referenced to **PCAF Standard (Section B61)**. The attribution is based on the bankÔÇÖs **market value holding** relative to the issuerÔÇÖs EVIC. Where a proxy input is required, **issuer revenue** is used as the proxy input in the calculation.
+
+The listed equity positions included in the 2024 financed emissions dataset are denominated in **EUR** and use **issuer revenue** as the proxy basis.
+
+**Selected listed equity holdingsÔÇö2024 (inputs used in the financed emissions approach)**
